 their outputs match, and EDT's answer comes out to cooperate, which is the essay's conclusion too.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working through the twin prisoner's dilemma under evidential decision theory, setting up the payoffs and expected utilities for cooperating versus defecting. Setting the two probabilities equal, the condition for cooperating comes out to p > 5/7, which matches the threshold in the essay. I'm now looking at how the correlation between the two twins enters the calculation.\n\nI'm checking the correlation argument: the two twins run the same reasoning, so their outputs match, and EDT's answer comes out to cooperate, which is the essay's conclusion too.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9806,"completion_tokens":693,"total_tokens":10499,"cost":0.053084,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.053084,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.039224,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01386},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":278,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}